# Action object fields used here: input[0]=unit type, input[8]=immediate action signal, input[9]=current terrain, input[10]=current resource value, input[11]=nearby resource score, input[12]=fresh-water flag, input[13]=city plot score or tactical usefulness, input[14]=age/pressure, input[15]=nearest friendly city distance.
# Local 9x9 window slots are input[16..96], scanned row-major from map offset di=-4,dj=-4 to di=+4,dj=+4. Slot input[56] is the center tile under this unit. Negative local values such as -0.200000 represent fog-of-war or unknown tiles.
# Forwarded strategy focus fields are relative to this unit: input[97]=target dx, input[98]=target dy, input[99]=military attack priority, input[100]=defense priority. dx/dy are normalized by the 9x9 window radius of 4 tiles.
# Cue meaning: center tile is forest with honey-like camp resource.
# Decision meaning: build improvement because camp is the matched resource improvement.
# Legal output candidates: output[0] = goto; output[1] = wait; output[3] = road to; output[4] = irrigate; output[5] = chop forest; output[6] = build improvement.
# Correct answer: choose output[6] = build improvement.
# Evaluation rule: after inference, compare only legal candidate outputs; the highest value is the predicted answer.
# Training target: output[6] is set to +0.900000, every other legal candidate output is set to -0.900000.
# input[0] = 0.062500 means unit type normalized as unitTypeIndex/32.
# input[9] = 0.750000 means current tile terrain type normalized as terrainType/8.
# input[8] = 0.800000 means immediate action signal: workers use 0.80 improvement, 0.60 irrigation, 0.45 chop, 0.30 road, 0.20 road-to; military uses 0.70 adjacent enemy, 0.50 defensive hill.
# input[56] = 0.840000 means main local 9x9 cue driving this action.
# input[99] = 0.000000 means forwarded strategy military attack priority.
# Machine row below repeats the same situation in parser format.
